      "extract": "\\label{sec1} It is now well established that Random Matrix Theory (RMT) accurately models spectral fluctuations in an abundant variety of different systems, such as chaotic, disordered and many--body systems, see the review in Ref.~\\cite{guhr97}. In recent years, RMT has in addition been successfully introduced into the study of certain aspects of Quantum Chromodynamics (QCD). The interest focuses on the spectral",
