      "extract": "\\label{sec311} In RMT one deals with an ensemble of matrices, where the matrix elements of each member are chosen randomly. Spectral observables predicted by RMT are calculated as an average over the ensemble. This ensemble average is denoted by a bar $\\overline{(\\ldots)}$. But observables can also be calculated as spectral average, i.e. one performs a running average over overlapping intervals $[\\alpha,\\alpha+L]$",
